# Strapi Cloud image upload (production)

## When images are missing on production

- Content/tenant links exist on Cloud, but cards show placeholders or broken images.
- `HEAD https://<cloud>/uploads/<file>` returns **404** while local `public/uploads/` works.
- Common cause: Cloud disk is **ephemeral** — DB still has `image.url` like `/uploads/...`, files wiped after deploy.
- Frontend (`mosc-temp`) resolves relative URLs via `NEXT_PUBLIC_STRAPI_URL` + `getMediaUrl` — fix Cloud files, not the Next app.

## Production vs demo tenant (critical)

| Audience | Tenant ID |
|---|---|
| Live site (`www.mosc-temp.com`, Amplify) | **`mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`** |
| Editor / demo CMS | `tenant_demo_002` |

Always pass `--tenant-id=` explicitly. In [scripts/lib/liturgy-cli.js](mdc:scripts/lib/liturgy-cli.js), **CLI flags override `.env` `TENANT_ID`** — confirm the log line `Tenant: mosc_malankara_orthodox_2` before trusting the run.

## Two upload strategies

### A — Quick fix (migration base64 → Cloud local disk)

Use when images 404 after deploy and you need production fixed now.

```bash
# Stop local Strapi first. Requires .env: STRAPI_CLOUD_URL, STRAPI_CLOUD_API_TOKEN
npm run finish:collection-images-on-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
```

- Success log looks like: `Created: 9 | Linked: 219`
- Windows may exit non-zero with `UV_HANDLE_CLOSING` after success — treat **Created/Linked** as the result.
- **Re-run after every Cloud deploy** (files land on ephemeral disk again).
- Batch: `npm run finish:all-collection-images-on-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`

### B — Durable fix (S3 + register-s3-media)

Prefer when Cloud has valid AWS vars and `UPLOAD_PROVIDER=aws-s3` (see [STRAPI_MEDIA_STORAGE_S3_CLOUD_PRD.html](mdc:documentation/STRAPI_MEDIA_STORAGE_S3_CLOUD_PRD.html)). Survives redeploys.

```bash
npm run push:collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
# optional: --skip-api  |  --skip-s3  |  --link-existing
npm run push:all-collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
```

Needs local `.env` AWS creds (`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_S3_BUCKET_NAME`) writing to the shared prod prefix. ACL: omit when bucket is “Bucket owner enforced” — [strapi-s3-upload-acl-fix.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/strapi-s3-upload-acl-fix.mdc).

## Script map

| Role | Path / npm script |
|---|---|
| Finish one collection (probe + push + verify) | [scripts/finish-collection-images-on-cloud.js](mdc:scripts/finish-collection-images-on-cloud.js) → `finish:collection-images-on-cloud` |
| Finish all registered collections | [scripts/finish-all-collection-images-on-cloud.js](mdc:scripts/finish-all-collection-images-on-cloud.js) → `finish:all-collection-images-on-cloud` |
| Base64 migration push | [scripts/push-collection-images-migration.js](mdc:scripts/push-collection-images-migration.js) (dedupes by file hash) |
| S3 push / register | [scripts/push-collection-images-s3-to-cloud.js](mdc:scripts/push-collection-images-s3-to-cloud.js) → `push:collection-images-s3-to-cloud` |
| Collection registry | [scripts/lib/cloud-image-migration-config.js](mdc:scripts/lib/cloud-image-migration-config.js) |
| Cloud endpoint (`uploadMedia`, `linkCollectionImages`, `register-s3-media`) | [src/index.js](mdc:src/index.js) |
| Upload provider config | [config/env/production/plugins.js](mdc:config/env/production/plugins.js) |

**`--collection` keys:** `catholicate`, `ecumenical`, `saints`, `publications`, `theological-seminaries`, `holy-synod`, `current-catholicos`, `institutions`, `training`, `spiritual-organisations`, `kalpana-editions`, `kalpana-documents`.

Content-first (if entries missing): `npm run push:<section>-to-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2` (e.g. `push:institutions-to-cloud`), then images via A or B.

## Workflow (institutions example — Jul 2026)

1. Confirm local has files under `public/uploads/` and Cloud entries exist for the **production** tenant.
2. Stop local Strapi.
3. Run strategy A (or B if S3 is ready):
   ```bash
   npm run finish:collection-images-on-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
   ```
4. Verify Cloud: with API token, `GET /api/institutions?populate=image` — every `image.url` should `HEAD` **200** (absolute Cloud URL for `/uploads/...`, or `https://...amazonaws.com/...` for S3).
5. Spot-check live page: `https://www.mosc-temp.com/mosc-redesign/institutions-cms` — card `<img>` src should point at Cloud/S3 and load.

## Agent invocation

- User: *“Upload / fix Cloud images for Institutions on production”* or *“re-run finish collection images for institutions”*
- Agent: run the command with **`mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`** unless user names another tenant; do not ask the user to run it.
- Read master doc: [cloud-image-upload-migration-fix.html](mdc:documentation/front_end_based_collection_types_import/production_cloud_data_push/cloud-image-upload-migration-fix.html) + per-type PRD under `documentation/front_end_based_collection_types_import/production_cloud_data_push/`.

## Adding a new collection

1. Register in [cloud-image-migration-config.js](mdc:scripts/lib/cloud-image-migration-config.js) (`uid`, `table`, `tenantLinkTable`, `entryIdCol`, `restPlural`, `mediaField`).
2. Document § Cloud image upload fix in the type’s `*-production-cloud-push-prd.html`.
3. Deploy Cloud if migration endpoints changed, then run finish/S3 for both tenants as needed.
